        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add auth list shortcut",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`openclaw models auth list` is the canonical command for inspecting saved model auth profiles, but the shorter top-level shape `openclaw auth list` is still unavailable. This PR adds only that shortcut and keeps the existing model-auth listing implementation as the source of truth.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add a top-level `openclaw auth list` command.\n- Delegate to the existing `modelsAuthListCommand`.\n- Preserve `--provider`, `--agent`, and `--json` behaviour.\n- Register the lazy top-level `auth` sub-CLI.\n- Document the shortcut in the CLI index and models auth docs.\n\n## Scope Boundary\n\n- No new auth storage, login, refresh, secret resolution, or provider probing behaviour.\n- No changes to `src/commands/models/auth-list.ts`.\n- This does not revive the stale #73462 branch; it is a fresh, narrow alias-only PR.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Local targeted Vitest did not run: this fresh worktree has no installed dependencies, and dependency verification could not reach npm registry endpoints (`ETIMEDOUT`/`ENOTFOUND`) before Vitest started. The branch is pushed for GitHub CI validation.\n\n## Security Impact\n\n- New permissions/capabilities: No.\n- Secrets/tokens handling changed: No.\n- New/changed network calls: No.\n- Command/tool execution surface changed: Yes, a read-only CLI alias is added.\n- Data access scope changed: No.\n\nThe alias reuses the existing redacted model auth profile listing command, so raw token/API-key/OAuth material remains hidden by the existing implementation and tests.\n",
